[Music]  this week's 48 hours investigates the  story of an american couple who adopted  a young girl from across the world and  came to fear her it began more than two  decades ago when the couple brought home  two children from russia they named the  nine-year-old girl cara lee the couple  came to believe carol lee was dangerous  even capable of murder they claimed she  tried to kill her little brother and  they took her right back to russia 48  hours contributor troy roberts covered  the story at the time and tried to keep  track of the young girl over the years  the two recently reconnected and robert  sat down with her to learn her  surprising story  how old were you when you were adopted  i was nine  and that's what i wanted  i want to feel loved and i want the  family  crystal and jesse we agreed not to use  their last name  first arrived in moscow russia in 1997  to adopt a girl they named cara lee and  a boy they named joshua when we finally  learned that we were going to be able to  go over to russia and pick up a little  boy and girl of our own it was just a  tremendous event and we were very  excited  how did the agency describe carolee  a wonderful outgoing intelligent little  girl but they say  carolee started behaving badly  not long after they returned home there  was a coldness in her and an anger and  just a distance she stole all my jewelry  our knives were disappearing and then  she snapped  they say  she tried to kill her baby brother she  had him in her hands and was going to  throw him over the deck she had him yes  yes over the side here yes and i just  started screaming put him down caroly  put him down what are you doing i'm  going to kill him dr brian kennedy was  one of the psychiatrists who saw carol  lee this child i would consider to be a  homicide risk we've had cameras  installed and we've had alarms installed  on her doors  so you plan on taking caroly back to  russia  yes yes i was with them 21 years ago  when they brought carol lee back to  russia  and left her there  you're a strong girl you're a strong  girl  i always wondered what became of her  and last summer we were reunited  and we learned what she says happened on  the deck that day and  about her incredible journey  troy roberts joins us right now troy how  did you finally find out what happened  to cara lee now sabrina  well we connected  on through social media  and  i asked her if she would want to tell me  her version of the events and so i went  to north carolina where she lives now  she's  a beautiful young woman married she has  four children wow and  uh well-adjusted she works at a hospital  and  um  she  it was painful for her to to review her  her life  but uh she says where she's at today  and her mental state  she's very grateful  how did troy how did it affect you  covering the story oh man um you know a  large part of our jobs  are to parachute into people's lives  when they're broken  you ask them  to tell their stories you say thank you  and you leave  and it was so hard for me to leave this  12 year old girl in a lot ward  in  a psychiatric hospital in moscow and i  was haunted uh  by this story  and  surprisingly it led to my own adoption  journey i  later adopted a four-year-old boy from  djibouti africa  he's now 23.  gets on my last nerve  as most kids  but troy i can hear the emotion in your  voice so thank you so much for covering  this and updating us on this story you  can see troy's report what happened to  the perfect child on 48 hours tomorrow  night at 10 9 central right here on cbs  and on the viacom cbs streaming service  paramount plus  we'll be right back

